Read at runtime:
```js
function readEnglish() {
  if (!fs.existsSync(enFile)) return {};
  return readCatalog(fs.readFileSync(enFile,'utf8'));
}
const EN = readEnglish();
```
But `readCatalog` is defined below; function declarations hoisted, fine. However, `EN` used in functions; can read inside functions to avoid stale. Use `readEnglish()` where needed.
- `readCatalog` currently parses first `{` to last `}`; `en.ts` has a `const en: Record<string,string> = { ... }`; first `{` is the object; last `}`; good.
- `message-ids.json` read in `checkProvenance` for validation.
- `community` file read:
```js
function readCommunity(locale) {
  const file = path.join(communityDir, `${locale}.ts`);
  if (!fs.existsSync(file)) return { ui: {}, monaco: {} };
  const data = readCatalog(fs.readFileSync(file,'utf8'));
  return { ui: data.ui ?? {}, monaco: data.monaco ?? {} };
}
```
- `readCommunityProvenance(locale)`:
```js
const file = path.join(communityDir, `${locale}.provenance.json`);
