Remove `vscodeMatches` variable, block, result; log line. Also perhaps validate that provenance `origins` has no orphan commit metadata? Not necessary, but we can add:
```
for (const origin of Object.keys(catalog.manifest.origins ?? {})) {
  if (![...used origins].includes(origin)) errors.push(... orphan origin)
}
```
But after generator prune, fine. Could add to prevent future dead metadata. However, `origins` map may include origins not used if a key removed; we want check to catch. The sidecar comparison already catches `community/<locale>.provenance.json` but `provenance.<locale>.json` `origins` map isn't compared? It is compared against generated `provenanceText`; generator prunes, so check fails. Good.

Orphan fix in `importCatalogs`:
```
const community = readCommunity(locale);
const origins = readCommunityOrigins(locale);
for (const id of Object.keys(origins)) if (!(id in community.ui)) delete origins[id];
```
Place after reading. Then missing origins. At end:
```
const usedOrigins = new Set(Object.values(origins));
const originsMap = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(existingProvenance.origins ?? {}).filter(([hash]) => usedOrigins.has(hash)));
```
But if a commit hash has metadata and used, keep. If missing, gitMetadata loop adds. Good.
Sidecar text uses `origins` pruned.
Note `origins` may be empty; okay.

Monaco check missing cache:
```
if (check) {
  if (fs.existsSync(target)) { ... } else { console.log(`  cache not present: ${...}`); }
}
```
Same override. But if cache absent, `generateMonacoMaps` still calls `fail` for invalid overrides. Good.
Change bottom call.

Remove `vscodeMatch` docs/code.

Let's apply code edits.

