commit 9f2458e77240545a017cd76fba3329be0ccb6980
Author: Luan Weslley <luanweslley77@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 22 14:28:40 2026 -0300

    Reload the editor when the locale changes

    Monaco resolves its NLS strings and the Calcpad editor actions are
    registered once, at startup. A live locale switch updated the Vue UI but
    left the editor menu in the previous language. Emit a locale-change event
    and let the desktop host flush drafts and the session before reloading the
    webview, so the editor comes back in the selected language.

