MenuItemAction label is a string snapshot at menu action creation. `MenuService.getMenuActions` builds actions and caches them until menu changes. If we mutate MenuRegistry item titles and fire change, new MenuItemAction labels update.

But retrieving all MenuRegistry items and mutating titles is doable. Need reverse translation map.

Yet many Monaco strings not in menus. Could at least update menus/command palette. The editor menus are the main complaint in commit. Maybe sufficient.

But the user objective says no reload, just render new translation. Could implement:
- Dynamic `__calcpadTr` with cache invalidation.
- On locale change:
  - Update all **registered menu item titles** and **command titles** by retranslating known strings.
  - Update all **editor actions** labels (`getSupportedActions`).
  - Re-add Calcpad actions (or update menu items directly covers context menu; internal action label used by command palette).
  - Refresh preview/diagnostics.
  - Update native menu.
  - No reload.
- Remaining stale: already-open widgets (find, suggest, hover) until reopened; module-scope strings in widgets. Could perhaps force close/reopen widgets; not necessary.

But how to translate existing labels? Build a reverse map at runtime. Let's design carefully.

### Vite virtual module changes

Current:
```
const __calcpadMaps = {...}; // only locales with monaco
let __calcpadResolved;
function __calcpadMatch(tag) ...
function __calcpadLocale() { if (__calcpadResolved) return ... }
export function __calcpadTr(module, key, english) {
  const map = __calcpadMaps[__calcpadLocale()];
  return map?.[module]?.[key] || english;
}
```

Add:
- `const __calcpadEnglish = new Map();` (English -> list of `module::key`)
- `const __calcpadReverse = new Map();` built lazily from maps: translated text -> set of `module::key` (for all locales). But reverse map from **old locale** only is enough for labels created in old locale; labels could be English (if old locale en). We can build reverse across all maps plus English registry.
- `__calcpadTr` records English mapping:
```
const id = module + '::' + key;
let set = __calcpadEnglish.get(english); if (!set) ...; set.add(id);
```
But this only records English strings for calls executed. Most menu labels executed at module init; good. For labels created after, also.
- Exports:
```
export function __calcpadSetLocale(tag) {
  __calcpadResolved = __calcpadMatch(tag) || 'en';
}
export function __calcpadTranslate(text, tag) {
  const target = __calcpadMaps[tag];
  if (!target) return undefined;
  const candidates = new Set();
  // find module/key by matching text in any map or English registry
  for (const map of Object.values(__calcpadMaps)) {
    for (const [module, entries] of Object.entries(map)) {
      for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(entries)) {
        if (value === text) candidates.add(module + '::' + key);
      }
    }
  }
  for (const [english, ids] of __calcpadEnglish) if (english === text) for (const id of ids) candidates.add(id);
  const translated = new Set();
  for (const candidate of candidates) {
    const [module, key] = candidate.split('::');
    const value = target[module]?.[key];
    if (value) translated.add(value);
  }
  return translated.size === 1 ? [...translated][0] : undefined;
}
```
But scanning all maps for every label on each locale change could be okay (1754*13 ~22k) once. Build a reverse map once:
```
let __calcpadReverse;
function __calcpadBuildReverse() { Map text -> Set(id) from all maps + English registry }
```
If `__calcpadTr` records English after reverse built, add entries dynamically.
- `__calcpadTranslate` could use reverse map. Need old text could be a translation in old locale; reverse map includes all locales. Ambiguity: if same translated text appears in multiple IDs with different target values, return undefined. If multiple IDs but same target value, return that value.
- Need handle labels with placeholders/params. Menu labels may have `{0}` etc.? `localize` with args formats; labels could contain dynamic text. Reverse exact match may fail if text includes dynamic values. For static menu labels, fine.
- English fallback: when target map lacks translation, target should fall back to English. We don't have English text for IDs unless `__calcpadEnglish` recorded; reverse map candidate can include English->ID, and target value missing -> use English. Need store ID->English map. `__calcpadTr` records `__calcpadEnglishById[id] = english`. Then `__calcpadTranslate` for candidate ID: `target[module][key] ?? __calcpadEnglishById[id]`.
- But `__calcpadTr` is called with English for each call; if same ID called with different English (rare), last wins. Fine.
- Also `__calcpadMaps.en` could be built from English strings? Not necessary.

Then `main.ts` imports `__calcpadSetLocale`, `__calcpadTranslate` from virtual module? The virtual module is not typed; add declaration? `vite.config.ts` virtual import currently only consumed via transformed Monaco code; app can import `virtual:calcpad-monaco-nls` if declaration. But `main.ts` could import from `'virtual:calcpad-monaco-nls'`; need `env.d.ts` declaration. Or expose via `monaco` global? Better add a small module `calcpad-web/src/i18n/monaco-nls.ts` that re-exports from virtual? Vite virtual import works if declaration. But `main.ts` is bundled; fine.
- However, the virtual module is currently private; adding import from app may cause it to be included; it already is. Fine.
- Add to `calcpad-web/src/env.d.ts` or `vite-env.d.ts`:
```
declare module 'virtual:calcpad-monaco-nls' {
  export function __calcpadSetLocale(tag: string): void;
  export function __calcpadRetranslate(text: string, tag: string): string | undefined;
}
```
- But `main.ts` import would be processed by Vite; okay.

### Updating Monaco labels

Option A: Update `MenuRegistry` internals directly. Import:
```
import { MenuRegistry, MenuRegistryChangeEvent } from 'monaco-editor/esm/vs/platform/actions/common/actions.js';
```
and `MenuId` maybe not needed; iterate `_menuItems` keys (MenuId objects). For each item:
- `item.command?.title`: string or `{value, original}`; `item.label` for submenu items; `item.command?.shortTitle` maybe.
- Retranslate `title` if string; if object with `value`, update `value`? Need mutate object property; `MenuItemAction` reads `.value` when constructing; if cached, fire change.
- `MenuRegistry._commands` command objects: `command.title` maybe string/object; update.
- Fire `MenuRegistry._onDidChangeMenu.fire(MenuRegistryChangeEvent.for(menuId))` for each menu key.
This is very internal; but can be done in a helper `retranslateMonacoMenus()`.

However, `MenuRegistry` import path may be aliased by monaco package; need verify same instance. Vite `resolve.alias` only calcpad-frontend; monaco internal path resolves from `calcpad-web/node_modules/monaco-editor/esm/...`. The app's `monaco-editor` import resolves to package main `esm/vs/editor/editor.main.js`; it imports `platform/actions/common/actions.js` with relative path -> same file. Our absolute import resolves to same file. Good.

But TypeScript may complain private fields; cast `as any`.

Option B: Re-add Calcpad actions and rely on `__calcpadTr` for new menus; built-in menus stale. Option A covers built-in.

Need update **editor action labels** for `getSupportedActions()` / command palette? `MenuRegistry` command items cover context menu and command palette; `editor.getAction(id).label` used by `trigger`? Maybe not. We can mutate `editor.getSupportedActions()` labels via `__calcpadRetranslate` too:
```
for (const editor of monaco.editor.getEditors()) {
  for (const action of editor.getSupportedActions()) {
    const translated = retranslate(action.label, locale)
    if (translated) action.label = translated; // readonly TS, cast
  }
}
```
Does `monaco.editor.getEditors()` exist? Check types.

