content.text:
Now write a CDP script. Need get websocket URL from `http://localhost:9222/json`. Use Node WebSocket global. Script can:
- connect to page target.
- `Runtime.enable`, `Page.enable`.
- Evaluate JS to wait for app/Monaco.
- Inspect DOM.

First, load page; get target. We'll write helper in `/tmp/opencode/cdp.mjs` maybe. But we need interact. Let's first get page info and evaluate basic state. Use shell with node heredoc. Node WebSocket messages; implement promise map.

CDP protocol:
```
const targets = await (await fetch('http://localhost:9222/json')).json();
const page = targets.find(t=>t.type==='page');
const ws = new WebSocket(page.webSocketDebuggerUrl);
await new Promise(res=>ws.onopen=res);
let id=0; const pending=new Map();
ws.onmessage = e => { const msg=JSON.parse(e.data); if(msg.id) pending.get(msg.id)?.(msg); };
function send(method, params={}) { return new Promise((res,rej)=>{ const i=++id; pending.set(i,()=>{pending.delete(i); res(msg)}); ws.send(JSON.stringify({id:i,method,params}));});}
```
Need handle events.
Evaluate:
```
await send('Runtime.evaluate',{expression:'document.title + "|" + document.querySelectorAll(".monaco-editor").length',returnByValue:true})
```
Let's inspect page.

